.env
# Secrets. data/ holds the API token, the saved settings (every provider key)
# and an optional cookies.txt. `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile would otherwise bake
# all of it into an image layer, where it survives every later deletion.
data/

# Node
node_modules/
dist/
web/dashboard/node_modules/
web/dashboard/dist/

# Session artifacts and git worktrees (6.6 GB here on 2026-09-24). The app never
# reads them; `COPY . .` and the `chown -R` after it copied every byte twice,
# which turned a rebuild into most of an hour. docker-compose bind-mounts the
# project anyway, so nothing inside the running container changes.
.claude/
